# Berlin booth

This workspace is the **Berlin** cut of the Uploadcare TV booth deck.
It was cloned from the Ecommerce Expo deck at `../ecommerce-expo`.

## Isolation

- Do **not** edit `../ecommerce-expo` or `../webflow-conf` from this chat.
- `origin` is the dedicated Berlin remote,
  `git@github.com:danieltroc-designer/uc-berlin.git`, branch `berlin`. Every
  push to it redeploys the public link, https://uc-berlin.vercel.app, so push
  only when the user asks. Never push to the Expo or Webflow remotes.
- The default deck is the four-card Berlin loop. The Ecommerce Expo and
  Webflow card types are still in the template but are not in the loop; do
  not reuse their copy, QR, or customer claims as Berlin facts.

## Build rules (unchanged)

- Edit `src/*.template.html` and `assets/`. Never hand-edit `dist/`.
- Rebuild with `python build.py` / `python build_simple.py` after source changes.
- Work in the booth loop (`src/simple.template.html`) unless asked for the
  full deck. Run `python tools/check_berlin.py` after changing a Berlin card.

## Event context

Read `EVENT.md` for confirmed vs TBD notes. When the user adds Berlin copy,
storyboard, QR, or giveaway details, update `EVENT.md` and the deck — do not
invent event facts.
